# ttychatter C changelog

## 0.4.0-c-cli

### Added
- Line-oriented interactive mode with `--interactive`
- Short `-i` alias for interactive mode
- Optional interactive session path argument
- Runtime colon-command system for the C client
- `:help` runtime command
- `:models` runtime command
- `:routers` runtime command
- `:update-models` runtime command
- `:test-model MODEL` runtime command
- `:model MODEL` runtime command for runtime model switching
- `:model-save MODEL` runtime command for runtime switch plus config save
- `:favorites`, `:favorite MODEL`, and `:unfavorite MODEL` runtime commands
- `:config`, `:set KEY VALUE`, and `:unset KEY` runtime commands
- `:set-api-key [gpg]` and `:forget-api-key` runtime commands
- `:memory` runtime command for viewing the active context buffer
- `:attach FILE`, `:attachments`, and `:clear-attachments` runtime commands
- `:editor` runtime command using VISUAL, EDITOR, or vi
- `:search TEXT` runtime command for current session search
- `:search-all TEXT` runtime command for SESSION_DIR search
- `:credits` runtime command
- `:doctor` runtime command
- `:quit` runtime command
- Literal-colon escaping with `\:`
- Interactive-mode documentation in README, WALKTHROUGH, and man page

### Changed
- Version updated to 0.4.0-c-cli
- C client parity with Bash runtime command mode improved
- Interactive mode reuses the same structured output/session file as file-in/file-out mode
- Interactive sends reuse attachment handling, context reconstruction, code-block extraction, and session append logic

### Notes
- Interactive mode is intentionally a line-oriented REPL, not a curses interface.
- The traditional `ttychatter input.txt output.log` workflow remains the default.
- Colon commands are local commands and are not sent to OpenRouter.

## 0.3.0-c-cli

### Added
- CONFIRM_LIVE_SEND config key
- --yes option for noninteractive confirmation bypass
- STARTUP_NOTICE config key
- New-output-file Project Lead notice block
- LOOPBACK config key
- THEME config key for cross-client config parity
- MODEL_SORT_ORDER config key
- --sort KEY model listing option
- --favorites-only model listing option
- Favorite marker column in model listings
- Model row sorting by name, context/tokens, type, or favorites
- Expanded --config output for new parity keys
- Expanded --doctor output for new parity keys
- Expanded man page documentation for confirmation, startup notice, loopback defaults, themes, model sorting, and favorites-only listing

### Changed
- Version updated to 0.3.0-c-cli
- Model listing now uses a model-row metadata structure instead of printing directly from JSON
- New output files can now include a non-context Project Lead notice block
- Live OpenRouter sends can be guarded by a confirmation prompt when configured
- Favorites are now visible in the model listing table

### Notes
- SEND_INPUT is intentionally not implemented because this C client is file-in/file-out by default.
- THEME is accepted for config parity but does not currently change command-line rendering.
- The Project Lead notice is not parsed as user or assistant context.

## 0.2.0-c-cli

### Added
- Demo mode with `--demo`
- Demo model list for offline/no-key testing
- Demo chat response for testing output/session/log behavior without network calls
- Demo model test support with `--demo --test-model MODEL`
- Config inspection command with `--config`
- Config write command with `--set KEY=VALUE`
- Config removal command with `--unset KEY`
- Model favorites file support
- `--favorites` command
- `--favorite-model MODEL` command
- `--unfavorite-model MODEL` command
- `MODEL_FAVORITES_FILE` config key
- `--loopback-file FILE` response mirroring

### Changed
- Version updated to `0.2.0-c-cli`
- `--update-models` writes the demo model cache when used with `--demo`
- `--models` can show local demo models when used with `--demo`
- `--test-model` no longer requires an API key in demo mode

## 0.1.0-c-cli

### Added
- Initial C command-line ttychatter client
- Traditional file-in/file-out workflow: `ttychatter input.txt output.log`
- OpenRouter chat-completions support through libcurl
- JSON request/response handling through json-c
- XDG-style config/cache/data defaults
- Config file loading from `~/.config/ttychatter/config`
- Environment API-key support through `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` and `TTYCHATTER_API_KEY`
- Plaintext API-key setup command
- Optional GPG-encrypted API-key setup command
- API-key forget command
- Doctor diagnostics command
- Model cache update command
- Model listing from cache
- Model search filter
- Model type filter for routers/fixed/free/auto
- Single-model test command
- Input file to output session log workflow
- Session continuation by reusing the same output file
- Context reconstruction from recent output-file turns
- Repeatable `--attach` / `-a` option
- Text attachment insertion
- Image attachment data URL support for compatible models
- Long fenced-code-block extraction into attachment files
- Loopback output mode for piping AI responses to stdout
- Traditional Unix man page
- Step-by-step WALKTHROUGH document
- Verbose maintainer comments in source code
